<Base title="About | Lokesh Jain"><div class="shell"><header class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">About the author</div><h1>Hi, I'm Lokesh.</h1><p>I'm a Dublin-based Senior MLOps Engineer who enjoys building the infrastructure behind production machine learning.</p></header><div class="prose"><p>My work spans distributed systems, ML platforms, and production AI infrastructure. Over more than a decade in software engineering, I've worked on distributed execution engines, reusable machine learning frameworks, and inference systems that process multimodal content.</p><p>Currently, at Integral Ad Science, I work on ML infrastructure, GPU-optimized multimodal classification, and active learning workflows. Previously, I worked on distributed execution systems at Blackswan Technologies and an internal ML framework at Noodle.ai.</p><p>This site is where I share engineering lessons, architecture trade-offs, practical examples, and experiments in inference, distributed systems, MLOps, and LLMOps. The writing reflects my own views; examples are generalized and don't disclose proprietary systems.</p><p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lokesh-jain-83a92b48/">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a> or <a href="mailto:lokeshjain927@gmail.com">get in touch by email ↗</a>.</p></div></div></Base>
